VERDICT (rf2-vc11), PR #9783. Option (b) taken.

WHAT MOVED: the six source-scanning pairs in docs.yml's `build` job moved verbatim into a new job, `source-scans` ("Docs source scans"). The pairs are EP status sync, runtime-subsystem grading, failure-corpus residue, retired composition vocab, retired EP-0026 image keys, and warm-allocation non-claim. All six are stdlib-only Python that read only the source tree. The new job has no `if:` on detect's output and no `needs:` on detect, so it runs on every PR. `build` keeps its `docs_surface` guard and now holds only build-site steps: the playground bundle build and smoke, the Cairo and MkDocs install, staging, `mkdocs build --strict`, and the upload.

WIRING: `source-scans` is in `docs-required`'s needs, so the aggregator grades it. It is also in `deploy`'s needs, so a red scan still blocks a Pages publish as it did from inside `build`.

BAND: +1 PR-time check, 87 to 88. docs.yml's pull_request trigger is unfiltered and the job is unconditional.

CLASS CLOSED: a path on push.paths but off detect's PR case list can now skip only the MkDocs build, never a scan. That covers implementation/machines/** (the #9748 incident), check_retired_image_keys.py and its fixtures, and skills/, which two of the scans read.

LIVE-CELL PATHS ANSWER: implementation/{core,adapters/reagent-slim,machines,flows}/** are NOT added to the case list. The build job does consume them through the playground SCI bundle's :local/root coords, but the MkDocs build proper does not read them. Their PR-time coverage is test.yml's tools-playground job. It runs the same `npm run build` and smoke of that bundle, and report-changed-surfaces.sh arms it for all four trees. Adding them here would duplicate a ~15-minute build on every core PR, which detect's own comment already rules out.

CONTROL: every moved scan was run locally. Each went RED against a planted fault that exists only in the worktree, and each named its own plant. The plants were:
- a new implementation/machines/src file carrying :rf.image/requires;
- a new testbeds file carrying :where :cofx;
- a new skills page with a live rf/realm call;
- EP-0001's index status flipped;
- the :rf.runtime/machines grading heading renamed;
- an unqualified per-write byte claim appended to CHANGELOG.md.

All went GREEN after a restore verified against the committed blob ids.

Workflow graders, all run locally and green: check_fast_pr_gap (79 to 80 required jobs, same unrun set), check_workflow_job_timeouts, _docs-workflow-policy.test.cjs, check_workflow_yaml and check_gate_scheduling. `mkdocs build --strict` also exited 0.

NOT DONE, ON PURPOSE (stance: one structural move): detect's case list and push.paths still carry entries that existed only to arm the scans. They now arm only the MkDocs build. Narrowing them is a possible follow-up, not a defect.

