description:
Mike asked on 2026-09-29 why workers re-run anything after a rebase, since CI has already graded the change and a PR with problems never merges. He is right, and the method already said so. docs/the-mayor-method/dispatch-prompt-template.md, around line 725 in the gate-menu section, reads: "So do not brief a re-run after a rebase ... push, and let CI's automatic re-run be the evidence about the new base."

PR #10621 (rf2-07nhp) then added a bullet to the "Before you push" section of the GATE-MECHANICS block (around line 920), which is pasted verbatim into every editing brief: "After a rebase, re-run only the suites the landing can REACH." That contradicts the menu, and because the block travels verbatim, every brief since carries the weaker rule.

MAYOR RULING (2026-09-29, on Mike's challenge): rewrite that one bullet so it agrees with the menu. The substance to carry:
- after a rebase, do not re-run locally: push, and let the change's CI be the evidence about the new base;
- the reason: CI grades the change merged onto the trunk as it stood at the push, and the merge criterion requires that run green, so a local re-run only duplicates it. The rf2-07nhp trial measured zero CI reds that a skipped re-run would have caught;
- quote in the change body that CI is the final-base gate, and never cite a pre-rebase local green as final;
- the one exception: a gate the change's CI never runs (nightly-only, or a local-only script the brief names as the gate), and only where the landing touches what it tests;
- keep the residual sentence: a sibling landing between a change's last CI run and its merge is covered by no re-run, only by the merge criterion's three-way merge and trunk CI after the merge.
Drop the reach-listing procedure and the "re-running changed the artefact" anecdote, which argue for the rule being retired. Keep the next bullet (diff against the merge base for reverts) unchanged.

Also check loops.md and the rest of the template for any other sentence prescribing a local re-run after a rebase, and align it the same way. Change nothing else.

